# Testing Standards

## Test Pyramid
Target distribution for engineering effort:
- Unit Tests: 60–70% (pure functions, domain logic)
- Integration Tests: 20–30% (real containers, HTTP)
- E2E Tests: 5–10% (Playwright, Cypress)

## Test Naming Convention
Test names MUST describe the scenario:
`test_<function_name>_<scenario>_<expected_result>`

Example: `test_get_user_when_user_not_found_raises_404`

## Mocking Boundaries
| Category | Rule |
|----------|------|
| External HTTP APIs | MUST mock at transport/network level |
| Databases | MUST use real technology via Testcontainers — in-memory replacements (H2, SQLite) are FORBIDDEN |
| Message Queues | MUST mock or use real broker via container |
| File System | SHOULD use temp directories |
| System Clock | MUST be injectable — never call `new Date()` or `System.currentTimeMillis()` directly |
| Value Objects | MUST NOT mock — instantiate real objects |
| Pure Functions | MUST NOT mock |
| Standard Library | MUST NOT mock |

## Real Container Mandate
Using H2 or any in-memory database to simulate PostgreSQL/MySQL is explicitly FORBIDDEN for integration tests. The database engine, query planner, and constraint enforcement differ — tests that pass on H2 routinely fail on the real database.

Use Testcontainers to run the real database in a disposable container. This is non-negotiable.

## Test Execution Time Contracts
| Test Type | Maximum Duration |
|-----------|------------------|
| Single unit test | < 100ms |
| Unit test suite | < 60s |
| Single integration test | < 30s |
| Full integration suite | < 10m |
| E2E smoke test | < 5m |

## Flaky Test Policy
Zero tolerance. A flaky test is worse than no test — it erodes trust in the entire suite.
- Flaky tests MUST be quarantined (tagged `@Disabled` / `skip`) within 24 hours of detection.
- Quarantined tests MUST be fixed or deleted within 72 hours.
- Flakiness root causes (time dependencies, shared state, race conditions, port conflicts) must be addressed — not hidden with retries.

## Test Independence
- Tests MUST NOT depend on execution order.
- Tests MUST NOT share mutable state.
- Each test MUST set up its own required state and clean up after itself.

## Coverage Targets
Coverage is a heuristic, not a goal. The RECOMMENDED minimum thresholds:
- Line coverage: ≥ 80%
- Branch coverage: ≥ 70%

Coverage MUST NOT decrease in a PR without an explicit documented justification.

